rclrs: build QoSProfile::best_available() inline instead of via the C extern static.

qos.rs references `rmw_qos_profile_best_available` as an `extern "C" static`
(bindgen), but in rmw/qos_profiles.h ALL the rmw_qos_profile_* values are
header-only `static const` (internal linkage) — none are exported by librmw.so.
Native (Linux) builds happen to resolve the extern because the toolchain keeps an
internal-linkage copy around; under the VxWorks clang/LLVM link (--gc-sections,
default visibility) that copy is dead-stripped everywhere, so there is no symbol to
bind and the node fails to link (undefined reference to
rmw_qos_profile_best_available).

rclrs already builds every OTHER qos profile (default/sensor_data/parameters/...)
inline in Rust; this makes best_available() consistent with its siblings, using the
same constants the C header defines (KEEP_LAST depth 10, all *_BEST_AVAILABLE
policies, default deadline/lifespan/lease). No behavior change on any platform.

--- a/src/qos.rs
+++ b/src/qos.rs
@@ -359,10 +359,19 @@
     /// > discovery.
     #[cfg(not(ros_distro = "humble"))]
     pub fn best_available() -> Self {
-        unsafe {
-            // SAFETY: There are no preconditions for using this static const
-            // global variable
-            (&rmw_qos_profile_best_available).into()
+        // VxWorks: the C `rmw_qos_profile_best_available` is a `static const` in
+        // rmw/qos_profiles.h (inline, per-TU), NOT an exported library symbol, so the
+        // bindgen `extern` reference has no provider. Build the profile inline from
+        // the same constants the C header uses.
+        QoSProfile {
+            history: QoSHistoryPolicy::KeepLast { depth: 10 },
+            reliability: QoSReliabilityPolicy::BestAvailable,
+            durability: QoSDurabilityPolicy::BestAvailable,
+            deadline: QoSDuration::SystemDefault,
+            lifespan: QoSDuration::SystemDefault,
+            liveliness: QoSLivelinessPolicy::BestAvailable,
+            liveliness_lease: QoSDuration::SystemDefault,
+            avoid_ros_namespace_conventions: false,
         }
     }
 }
